{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-spectral-sequence-collapse","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:spectral-sequence-collapse","kind":"proposition","title":"GB spectral sequence collapses at E_1 (semisimple cohomology vanishing)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-curvature-rank-gb-stratification"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.WedderburnMass.centralIdempotent_idem","text":"spectral-sequence-collapse.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:spectral-sequence-collapse\"></a><p><em>For semisimple <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = H_n(R, q)</code>, Hochschild cohomology vanishes in positive degrees <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{HH}^k(A,\\, A) = 0</code>. The GB filtration spectral sequence collapses at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_1</code>, concentrating all contributions in the center <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_\\infty^{0, *} = Z(A)</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.24.11"}
